f Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and January to February and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, January to February came in at 44% of normal and August to September at 56%. So far in 2026, March to April hit 224% of normal on the middle of the grids, while May to June and June to July each came in at 72%. Grid 28079 had its driest year in 1958 at 66% of normal.</p>"}
